WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.420
<v ->How do we accomplish what needs to get done</v>

2
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.520
when an easier or more appealing option exists?

3
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.060
For example why don't we always sleep in,

4
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.490
binge watch tv, or leave work early?

5
00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.450
The answer comes down to motivation.

6
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.420
Motivation is what inspires us to act

7
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.483
and it comes from many sources.

8
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.780
There are three primary types of motivators.

9
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:33.740
First we might be motivated by a sense of obligation,

10
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.723
such as when we attend a party we'd rather not go to.

11
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:41.460
Or we might be inspired by extrinsic motivators

12
00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.260
that come from outside.

13
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.780
We push ahead because we expect a reward or recognition.

14
00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.870
And finally we might be motivated by intrinsic factors

15
00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.880
that come from within.

16
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.150
Self-motivation is intrinsic.

17
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.200
We work towards personal results

18
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.103
rather than external rewards.

19
00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:04.460
With self-motivation you can use your emotions

20
00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.590
as drivers to push you toward your goals

21
00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:08.600
and remain resilient.

22
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.420
Of all the motivators it's the most stable

23
00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.360
since it's something that only you can control.

24
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.400
No one else can give it or take it away.

25
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.320
So let's take a look at some of the personal

26
00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:23.410
and leadership benefits of self-motivation

27
00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.783
as well as how you can improve the skills.

28
00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.240
The first benefit of self-motivation

29
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.990
is that it's associated with an achievement drive.

30
00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.090
You're driven to create challenging goals

31
00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.973
and work towards those objectives.

32
00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.780
And as a leader that helps you set

33
00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.080
a standard of excellence, avoid complacency,

34
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.970
and inspire your staff with future-focused vision.

35
00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:50.650
Second, with high self-motivation you're also likely

36
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.930
to have a high sense of commitment and follow through.

37
00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:56.300
You're willing to make sacrifices for your goals

38
00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.660
and that helps you earn a team confidence.

39
00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:03.350
Third, with self-motivation you're also more likely

40
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.840
to take the initiative.

41
00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:08.710
So rather than waiting for opportunities to come to you,

42
00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:11.330
you'll proactively seek them out.

43
00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:15.240
And as a leader, that mentality can help you take charge

44
00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.400
and push your team to action.

45
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.830
And finally self-motivation cultivates optimism.

46
00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:24.280
Rather than giving up when faced with setbacks,

47
00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.030
you persevere and work through obstacles

48
00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:30.520
and that can inspire others to adopt the same mindset

49
00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.880
and push past their own temporary hiccups.

50
00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.160
There are several strategies you can follow

51
00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.490
to increase your self-motivation.

52
00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.653
Here are five well known techniques.

53
00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:44.820
The first strategy for increasing your self-motivation

54
00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.750
is to define your why's.

55
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.520
If you can't remember why you're making sacrifices,

56
00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.830
then it's difficult to keep going.

57
00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.930
So spend sometime thinking about what inspires you.

58
00:02:55.930 --> 00:03:00.000
Consider your career, family, finance,

59
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.370
health, social, and spiritual goals.

60
00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.310
Next break down SMART goals.

61
00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:08.380
Come up with a definite objective

62
00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.140
and then break that objective down

63
00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.490
into smaller attainable pieces.

64
00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:14.880
Keep those goals SMART by ensuring

65
00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.510
that they're specific, measurable, attainable,

66
00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.210
realistic, and time-based.

67
00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.590
Third, celebrate wins along the way.

68
00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.330
Don't just focus on the reward at the finish line.

69
00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:31.360
The next time you meet a milestone recognize that success,

70
00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:35.450
feel proud, and allow yourself to indulge in a small reward

71
00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.940
such as a trip to the movies or a night out with friends.

72
00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.800
Fourth, don't compare yourself to others.

73
00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.100
Comparisons only waste time

74
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.250
and paint an unrealistic picture of reality.

75
00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.520
Instead look within.

76
00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.250
Look at where you've been and how you've improved.

77
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.230
Only compare yourself to yourself.

78
00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:58.850
And finally control your internal self-talk.

79
00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.130
We all have an inner voice

80
00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.460
that's constantly feeding us information,

81
00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.040
some positive and some negative.

82
00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.050
To maintain motivation control that self-talk

83
00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:11.690
so that it acts as a coach rather than a critic.

84
00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:15.173
Tell yourself my goals are possible.

85
00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:19.070
The key to self-motivation is remembering

86
00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.690
that it's up to you to determine what happens.

87
00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.330
You are in control.

88
00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.820
And if you feel like you're falling off track,

89
00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.990
remember the tips we just covered.

90
00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.260
Follow these strategies and you can bring

91
00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.613
your goals to fruition.

